1
00:00:00,841 --> 00:00:03,541
(Sheldon:)Raj, now, I'm sorry
you're suffering.

2
00:00:03,544 --> 00:00:06,744
(Sheldon:)When Amy and I were
broken up, I also suffered.

3
00:00:06,747 --> 00:00:09,117
(Sheldon:)And this may
sound surprising,

4
00:00:09,116 --> 00:00:11,486
(Sheldon:)but I'm grateful for
having gone through it.

5
00:00:11,485 --> 00:00:13,485
(Bernadette:)Really?

6
00:00:13,487 --> 00:00:15,517
(Sheldon:)Yes.

7
00:00:15,522 --> 00:00:19,892
(Sheldon:)I believe our relationship
now is stronger than ever.

8
00:00:19,893 --> 00:00:22,493
(Amy:)So do I.

9
00:00:22,496 --> 00:00:23,926
When-when we were apart,

10
00:00:23,931 --> 00:00:26,101
(Sheldon:)I learned how important
you are to me.

11
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:28,269
(Sheldon:)And I realize

12
00:00:28,268 --> 00:00:30,868
(Sheldon:)that when two people are
in love, sometimes they...

13
00:00:30,871 --> 00:00:33,041
BOTH:
Happy Valentine's Day!

14
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:36,880
(whooping)

15
00:00:36,877 --> 00:00:39,277
We are young and fun!

16
00:00:39,279 --> 00:00:43,019
(horn honking)

17
00:00:44,585 --> 00:00:46,615
(Sheldon:)I stand corrected.

18
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,120
Fun.

19
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:58,280
(Sheldon:)Congratulations on a
successful live show.

20
00:00:58,277 --> 00:01:01,007
(Amy:)And a lovely
Valentine's Day.

21
00:01:03,048 --> 00:01:07,248
(Penny:)Cleaning up
is not young and fun.

22
00:01:07,252 --> 00:01:09,482
(Leonard:)It can be.
Confetti fight!

23
00:01:14,627 --> 00:01:16,697
(Leonard:)Maybe you should take a break.

24
00:01:16,695 --> 00:01:18,225
(Leonard:)I got this.

25
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:26,033
(Sheldon:)Did you know the singular
of confetti is "confetto"?

26
00:01:26,038 --> 00:01:29,878
(Amy:)Interesting, and when
would you use the singular?

27
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:30,945
(Sheldon:)I'm glad you asked.

28
00:01:30,943 --> 00:01:34,013
(Sheldon:)Amy, you have a
confetto in your nose.

29
00:01:34,013 --> 00:01:37,223
(Sheldon:)No, no, no, no. Other
side. There you go.

